  "checkpoint_text": "Step 1: Calculate $(3.6)^2$.\nStep 2: Apply the ceiling function to the result of step 1.\nStep 3: Determine $\\lceil 3.6 \\rceil$.\nStep 4: Square the result from step 3.\nStep 5: Subtract the result of step 4 from the result of step 2.\n\nFirst, calculate $(3.6)^2 = 12.96$.\nThen, apply the ceiling function to $12.96$, which gives $\\lceil 12.96 \\rceil = 13$.\nNext, determine $\\lceil 3.6 \\rceil = 4$.\nSquare this value to get $4^2 = 16$.\nFinally, subtract $16$ from $13$ to get $13 - 16 = -3$.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{-3}",
